❓Question
You are given an integer array height.
Each element represents the height of a vertical line. Find two lines that can form a container containing the maximum amount of water.
The container cannot be slanted.

Example
For:
height = [1,8,6,2,5,4,8,3,7]
The maximum area is:
49
because the lines with heights 8 and 7 are 7 units apart:
width = 8
height = min(8,7) = 7
area = 8 × 7 = 56
Correction: for the standard example, the indices are 1 and 8, so the width is 7 and:
area = 7 × 7 = 49

✅Approach
Use the two-pointer approach.
start starts from the left.
end starts from the right.

Calculate:

width = end - start
height = minimum of both heights
area = width × height
Store the maximum area.
Move the pointer having the smaller height because the smaller line limits the water level.
In your code, when both heights are equal, you move end.

Code
class Solution {
    public int maxArea(int[] height) {
        int start = 0;
        int end = height.length - 1;
        int sum = 0;
        while(start < end) {
            int diff = end - start;
            int min = Math.min(height[start], height[end]);
            if(sum < diff * min) {
                sum = diff * min;
            }
            if(height[start] > height[end] || height[start] == height[end]) {
                end--;
            } else {
                start++;
            }
        }
        return sum;
    }
}

Time Complexity
O(n)
Space Complexity
O(1)
